  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1150 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nThe main concern today through Friday afternoon will be fire \nweather, primarily west river where min RH falls to 15 to 25 percent \nin portions of the area each day. Winds will be marginal this \nafternoon and Thursday afternoon, but will need to keep a close eye \non Corson county for Thursday as the southwest winds pick up. \n\nOn Friday, winds will shift to the north behind a cold fropa and \ngust 30 to 40 mph. Still looking at fire weather concerns for areas \nsouth of Pierre and west of Lower Brule where fuels are burnable. \nWell above normal temps in the 80s are expected to fall sharply \nbehind the front with highs on Saturday topping out in the upper 60s \nto lower 70s. Fall-like temps are then forecast through the middle \nof next week. \n\nWith that cold fropa on Friday, the best moisture convergence, CAPE \nand forcing set up ahead of the low in Minnesota. However, there is \nstill a slight risk outlook as far west as I-29. Given the steep \nlapse rates with the drier mid level air, strong winds would be the \nbiggest threat. \n\nAn upper trough and sfc low move through the northern Plains Sunday \nand Monday bringing more widespread rain to the region. Current QPF \nforecast ranges from half an inch to 1.5 inches. High pressure then \nbuilds in to round out the next 7 days.",
